WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Shake a jar of river
water, then set it down.

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.990
Within seconds, the sand
has dropped to the bottom.

3
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:12.750
But the water stays cloudy for hours, full
of fine silt that seems to hang there.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.560
Both sink through the same still water.

5
00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.080
So why is the silt so slow?

6
00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:22.900
In this mission, you'll meet
viscosity: a fluid's internal friction.

7
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.610
High in honey, low in water.

8
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.620
Then you'll balance the three forces
on a sphere sinking through oil,

9
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.610
and find the steady speed it settles into.

10
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:37.880
Your mission: explain why fine silt
settles so much more slowly than sand.
